noether 0.1
## Research task: the Toffoli gate over Clifford+T with the smallest T-depth.
##
## A candidate defines Toffoli3_{r[3]} (r[0], r[1] controls, r[2] target). It is lowered into
## {H, S, S†, T, T†, CNOT} and must match Toffoli up to global phase (average gate fidelity
## ≥ 0.999999). Objectives, in order: T-depth, then T-count, then CNOT count.
## The goal T-depth ≤ 3 is the known optimum without ancillas (7 T gates). The textbook
## decomposition reaches T-depth 4.
##
## Try it with
##     noether check toffoli_tdepth_algo.ntr --spec toffoli_tdepth_spec.ntr
##     noether eval --spec toffoli_tdepth_spec.ntr --candidate toffoli_tdepth_algo.ntr
## or start an autoresearch workspace with
##     noether research init toffoli --spec toffoli_tdepth_spec.ntr --from toffoli_tdepth_algo.ntr
task "toffoli-tdepth"
qubits q[3]
candidate def Toffoli3_{q[3]}
target unitary Toffoli_{q[0], q[1]→q[2]}
gates {H, S, S†, T, T†, CNOT}
coupling all
readout exact
require fidelity ≥ 0.999999
minimize tdepth
minimize tcount
minimize count2q
goal tdepth ≤ 3
budget experiments=40, wall=30m
